Description: Derive plane layout for NC12 (SAND128 column-tiled) in V4L2FormatToVideoFrameLayout
 The Pi 5 HEVC decoder (rpi-hevc-dec) outputs NC12 (semi-planar 8-bit) in a
 single dmabuf laid out as Broadcom SAND128 (column-tiled). When chromium's
 V4L2FormatToVideoFrameLayout encounters NC12 with num_buffers=1 and
 num_color_planes=2, the switch falls through to the default branch and
 returns nullopt with "Cannot derive stride for each plane for pixel format
 NC12". The PlatformVideoFramePool then has no FrameResource to hand to the
 V4L2StatelessVideoDecoderBackend.
 .
 SAND128 layout: the buffer is split into 128-byte-wide vertical columns;
 each column contains the Y rows (height) stacked above the CbCr rows
 (height/2). V4L2 reports `bytesperline` as the per-column line count
 (which Mesa later uses as `sand_col128_stride`). The chroma plane lives
 at fixed offset `height * 128` from the start of the buffer (within the
 first column), regardless of width. Linear NV12 math (`stride * height`)
 produces the wrong chroma offset and was shown in prior iterations to
 cause magenta/green chroma banding at column boundaries.
 .
 Gate on BUILDFLAG(USE_V4L2_CODEC_RPI) since SAND128 is Broadcom-specific.
Author: Sean Slivinski <sslivins@microsoft.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-05-04
--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_utils.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_utils.cc
@@ -286,6 +286,26 @@
     // It is safe to cast to size_t.
     const size_t y_stride_abs = static_cast<size_t>(y_stride);
     switch (pix_fmt) {
+#if BUILDFLAG(USE_V4L2_CODEC_RPI)
+#ifndef V4L2_PIX_FMT_NC12
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_NC12 v4l2_fourcc('N', 'C', '1', '2')
+#endif
+      case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NC12: {
+        // NC12 is semi-planar with Broadcom SAND128 column-tile layout. The
+        // chroma plane lives at offset (height * 128) within the first
+        // column, NOT at (y_stride * height) -- y_stride here is the
+        // per-column line count reported via bytesperline, not a normal
+        // linear stride.
+        const size_t sand128_chroma_offset =
+            static_cast<size_t>(pix_mp.height) * 128u;
+        const size_t sand128_chroma_size =
+            (static_cast<size_t>(pix_mp.height) / 2u) * 128u;
+        planes.emplace_back(y_stride, sand128_chroma_offset,
+                            sand128_chroma_size);
+        DCHECK_EQ(2u, planes.size());
+        break;
+      }
+#endif
       case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12:
         // The stride of UV is the same as Y in NV12.
         // The height is half of Y plane.
